      children: "Turning our attention to B5 T1 and I6 AC5, observe the speed interactions between the two on the first two turns: on Turn 1, I6 AC5 uses Tailwind before B5 T1 moves, while on Turn 2 B5 T1 uses Taunt before I6 AC5 moves. Therefore either Tailwind or Taunt must have been used with increased priority. However, the only way Taunt's priority could have been boosted is with Prankster, but if this was so then Taunt would not have successfully landed on Incineroar on Turn 2 (since Dark-type Pokémon are immune to Prankster-boosted moves). Therefore Tailwind must have been boosted in a way besides Prankster (otherwise Prankster would still be active on Turn 2). The only possibility is that it was boosted by Gale Wings, the signature ability of Talonflame. Therefore one of B5 T1 and I6 AC5 must be Talonflame, and the other must have access to Toxic Spikes as used on Turn 2."
